          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Each day, Bob has a 25% chance of being late. Assume that being late on different days is independent. Find the probability, correct to three decimal places, that on five consecutive days:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p24-q16-a-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Bob is not late on any day.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.237$",
          "worked": "The probability of being on time on one day is $1-0.25=0.75$. The days are independent.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{not late on any day})&=(0.75)^5\\\\P(\\text{not late on any day})&=\\frac{243}{1024}\\\\P(\\text{not late on any day})&\\approx0.237\\quad\\text{(3 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p24-q16-b-prompt",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Bob is late on at least one day.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.763$",
          "worked": "Use the complement of not being late on any day.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{late on at least one day})&=1-(0.75)^5\\\\P(\\text{late on at least one day})&=\\frac{781}{1024}\\\\P(\\text{late on at least one day})&\\approx0.763\\quad\\text{(3 d.p.)}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
